rooms_desc ({"You have just entered the magnificent mansion that is Gothrog's houseA portal to the church (tastefully done in oak) is hereEntrances to the east and west wings are here","This is the entrance to the east wing. It has a high vaultedceiling and many tapestries hang on the walls.A strong light comes from the south","This is the entrance to the west wing. Fine tapestries adorn the wallstogether with pictures of Gothrog's ancestors. It all looks rather sombreand dark. The room is lit by a candleabre hanging from the ceiling","This is the west wing drawing room where Gothrog entertains his guestsTwo red leatherbound armchairs and a red leatherbound sofa are arrangedaround a genuine Dunedain iron fireplace. A fire burns merrily inthe grate. In the corner is a drinks cabinet and a bell pull","Upon entering this room you have to immediately shield your eyes - thelight is blinding in here. As your eyes adjust, you begin to make outimmense pillars of pure amethyst stretching up to the roof. A table ofclear quartz floats here, with a bowl brimming over with exotic fruitssitting on it.","This is the library where Gothrog comes to study during exams. The wallsare lined with ancient tomes detailing the three ages. A highly polishedscimitar hangs on one wall","This is the banquetting hall where Gothrog eats and drinks. Looking up,you can see the blackened oak beams of the roof. A long elm table is hereon which stand two huge brass candlesticksA passageway to the kitchen (south) is sectioned off by a velvet curtain.","This room returns to the more traditional style to which Gothrog isaccustomed. A large four poster is centred against the east wall, with adoor to the bathroom set alongside. The south wall contains a fireplaceand two large lead latticed windows look out onto the lawn","This is the bathroom off the master bedroom. The tub is HUGE, with bubblesmagically arising from the bottom effervessing furiously at the surface.A comfy leather lav. is here as well, for when gothrog wants to contemplatelife, and a large washbasin and mirror are attached to the south wall","Upon entering the kitchen, your nose is assaulted by the rich spicy smellscoming from the cooking of unfamilar meats and puddings. There is a largestove in the corner of room and a large fireplace contains a spit on whichis roasting a large haunch of venison. The atmosphere is dark and smoky.",})
